# Browser
# Bot2 casts Dispelling Exhale at Bot1's Lightning Bolt and beholds the Kokusho in its hand (CR 701.4a): the card is revealed, so while
# the Exhale is on the stack Bot1's page shows it among the cards known in Bot2's hand and says so in its game log ("Bot2 reveals
# Kokusho, the Evening Star"); it knew nothing of Bot2's hand before and, a step later, shows it hidden again. Bot1 cannot pay {4}
# and declines. The log does not call the spell "kicked": behold is no kicker.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Lightning Bolt
Mountain x5
Mountain x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Sapphire
Kokusho, the Evening Star
Dispelling Exhale
Island x3
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
? Client.Bot1.OpponentHand =
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire#2.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dispelling Exhale.Cast
Bot2.Modes(Behold a Dragon)
Bot2.Target(Stack.Lightning Bolt)
Bot2.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot2.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot2.Choose(Kokusho, the Evening Star)
? Client.Bot1.OpponentHand = Kokusho, the Evening Star
? Client.Bot1.Log.Has = Bot2 reveals [Kokusho, the Evening Star].
? Client.Bot1.Log.Has = Bot2 casts [Dispelling Exhale] targeting [Lightning Bolt].
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.OpponentHand =
Bot1.Decline
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Revealed = Kokusho, the Evening Star
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
